   "brief": [
    "Goal: close the delta review of kitchen `40378ef..22caa8d` so the line can be accepted. Work in the nested clone `.cache/kitchen/repo` (local main, HEAD `22caa8d`). Read the review first: `<review drop>/KITCHEN-DELTA-REVIEW-22caa8d/report.md`. Its probes are in the same directory.",
    "Vasyl's decision (poll 2535): bump the contract to `kitchen-cook-adapter/2`. The reviewer showed that a fresh per-request Bun cache can resolve unpinned ranges to newer versions. So \"the new names don't change what enters the build\" is false, and the `/1` exception goes. Record the `/2` contract and update the port notes and D5 text honestly: the fresh-cache acquisition is part of the contract. All four live agents will get a new build name and will rebuild once, in the later thin-Ansible window. That is accepted. Don't try to avoid it.",
    "W1. The takeover witness: must include each build's own root directory metadata; in read-only `verify`, must also inventory the requested/current build; must treat unreadable-error markers as incomplete measurement, not unchanged. The emitted `measured`/`not_measured` must state exactly what is covered.",
    "Local git. A connector cloned from a local repository hard-links git objects across builds, and kitchen then refuses a legitimate build. If cook can be made to clone with `--no-hardlinks` through what the adapter controls, do that. If not without changing cook, keep the refusal and document it clearly as a known limitation, with the cook change as backlog. Don't weaken the shared-inode check.",
    "Also, if cheap: clean up orphaned `ROOT/.bun-cache-*` from killed runs, for example at the start of any prepare for that root. Otherwise backlog it."
