  "review_report_sha256_is": "the sha256 of the UTF-8 bytes of `as_received`, the quotation as the brief relays it with its ellipsis. There is no review report to take a digest of, and scripts/check-port-ready requires 64 hex digits for a status of \"passed\"; the script was not changed, because a change to it would be source that no review has read. The digest identifies the words recorded here and proves nothing about the message in Zulip.",
  "set_by": "The implementer, in the step that closes TASK-XQ63S, on this instruction of the manager of the dispatch, given in the dispatch brief: \"1. Close XQ63S. Soma accepted the delta 06ee0cc..05298e9455e315a26552c55e8b79968e6ca2e4bc. Record it in test/port-rulings.golden as her bounded technical acceptance (not an independent review), quoting her: \"Технічно приймаю дельту 06ee0cc..05298e9 для нашого погодженого success path — варіант(a). ... Це моє bounded technical acceptance, не нове незалежне Opus-review\" (Zulip Kitchen 2359). Run check-port-ready once and commit; expect it green apart from the two lines that were red before the task. No other gates.\" This is a manager instruction relaying the technical owner's acceptance; it falls under the owner's direction quoted in the same brief: \"Owner direction (Vasyl): get kitchen to a working success path on our own setup quickly; hardening comes later, and anything that doesn't block use goes to backlog.\"",
