  "not_covered": "Everything committed after 05298e9. The commit that records this acceptance changes only this file and docs/, which the readiness check prints as a NOTE and does not block on. The corpus harness of task B, committed after it, is new source outside docs/ that neither a review nor this acceptance has read, and scripts/check-port-ready blocks on it until it has a review or an acceptance of its own.",
  "rule": "A status of \"passed\" names the commit reviewed and the sha256 of the review report. It is set by a reviewer, or by the implementer on a quoted instruction, never on the implementer's own judgement. `set_by` quotes the instruction and says whose it is: the technical owner's for the review of a198042, the manager's for the reviews of 621d78d and of 06ee0cc (see earlier_delta_reviews for all three). This entry is the one exception to the first sentence, and says so in `kind`, `review` and `review_report_sha256_is`: it records an acceptance by the technical owner in place of a review, on the manager's quoted instruction."
