   "id": "L1",
   "subject": "review finding",
   "as_received": "Review L1. Close the second-pass gap: have `scan` record per-step (length, crc32) and have GzipSource fail closed on a mismatch, or argue why that is not worth it and narrow the wording. Your call. L2 (raw crashes under engine change) can stay as a B9 note.",
   "left_to_the_implementer": "Close the gap or narrow the wording. Chosen: close it.",
   "bounds": [
    "The checking pass records, for every piece of output, its length and the CRC-32 of its member up to and including it: eight bytes per step. Every later pass over the container (the listing, a backward seek, a member read) is held to that record piece by piece, and a member must end after the same number of steps at the same byte of the file.",
    "A later pass that differs ends in `UnsupportedRuntime`, as does damage reported in a later pass: the archive has passed its check by then, so the fault is the engine's and is not answered as \"unreadable archive\".",
    "What the record does not cover is a fault that changes a piece and leaves both its length and the running CRC-32 as they were.",
    "L2 stays as it was ruled, a note on B9: an engine whose errors arrive only asynchronously would end in an unhandled `error` event, a crash and not a refusal."
   ],
   "evidence": [
    "src/pylike/tarfile.ts (StepRecord, GzipSource)",
    "test/unit/port-runtime.test.js (faults injected into the stepwise call)"
   ]
